      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Reuse Existing Classes\n\nThe following classes from the Person Template should remain valid for organizations:\n\n- `role`\n- `life-event`\n- `relationship`\n- `work`\n- `media`\n- `claim`\n- `evidence`\n- `source`\n- `quote`\n\nExamples:\n\n- A founder or executive holds a `role`.\n- A merger or bankruptcy is a `life-event`.\n- A partnership or ownership link is a `relationship`.\n- A report, publication, or software project may be a `work`.\n- Public statements may be represented by `quote` nodes.\n- Contested assertions remain `claim` nodes supported by `evidence` and `source` nodes.\n\nThis shared vocabulary allows Person and Organization graphs to interoperate naturally.\n\n## Compatibility correction\n\n`relationship` is generalized to a typed directional connection between two entities. `role` names a position or office; `affiliation` records who or what participates in the organization, optionally through that role.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784473618170,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
