      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# New Class: `affiliation`\n\nAffiliation is the most important organization-specific addition.\n\nIt represents a temporal, sourced connection between a person or organization and an organization.\n\n## Suggested fields\n\n- Affiliation kind\n- Title or capacity\n- Start date\n- End date\n- Active status\n- Notes\n\n## Example kinds\n\n- Founder\n- Employee\n- Executive\n- Board member\n- Member\n- Donor\n- Contractor\n- Partner\n- Affiliate\n\n## Shape\n\n`Person → Affiliation → Organization`\n\nor\n\n`Organization → Affiliation → Organization`\n\nA dedicated affiliation class prevents common organizational relationships from collapsing into vague labels while preserving dates, roles, and evidence.\n\n## Boundary\n\nUse `affiliation` for membership, employment, leadership, board service, contracting, or participation. Use `relationship` for parent/subsidiary, ownership, partnership, alliance, and other entity-to-entity structure. Provenance belongs in connected Claim → Evidence → Source nodes.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784473618170,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
