        "markdown": "# Candidate Class: `offering`\n\nOrganizations produce and operate many kinds of things:\n\n- Products\n- Services\n- Programs\n- Campaigns\n- Initiatives\n- Platforms\n- Publications\n- Grants\n\nA broad `offering` class could represent these initially, using a `kind` field to distinguish them.\n\n## Suggested fields\n\n- Name\n- Kind\n- Description\n- Launch date\n- End date\n- Status\n- Website\n- Owning organization\n\nThis class should remain provisional. Existing `work` nodes may already cover publications, software, and creative output. The first implementation should avoid duplicating `work` unless concrete examples expose a real semantic gap.\n\n## Version-one decision\n\nDeferred. Use `work` only where it remains semantically honest, and add `offering` after the OpenAI validation case demonstrates the boundary for products, services, grants, and programs.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784473618170,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
